A||||9||Shiner||Yellow fiero owners here?||||5||
Z||000000||Shiner||02-13-2000||02:54 AM||||Okay, you may remember my post awhile back, asking for opinions on what color to paint my car ('87 GT)  I was thinking red with gold wheels was my finaly choice.  But I took a look around, and you know what?  There is an incredible amount of red cars of the road!  Now, I know certain fiero forum members would disagree with me (not naming names... you know who you are...lol) on this, but I was thinking of yellow.  Not the stock yellow, mind you, but the type of yellow that they paint new mustangs, you know, Lotus yellow.  <P> So, does anybody here own a yellow GT?  Does it get a lot of attention from passerby and police officers?  I like attention, (don't we all?), but I do not want to be pulled over and harassed by every Pensy State trooper I pass!  So, tell me what it's like to drive a yellow GT!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||02-13-2000||06:02 AM||||I don't have a GT but I just had my Formula painted Corvette Competition Yellow and to me and many others it looks quite nice. When I told some people that I was going to paint it yellow I got a lot of "yellow???", but when they saw the finished product they were impressed. When the slop gets off the roads and I can get it washed I will post pics||||reg||1
Z||000002||mutfish||02-13-2000||10:06 AM||||If you decide to go with yellow, take a look at "1977 corvette  bright yellow",it really "pops". I painted my '72 with it and get tons of compliments, I think it's an outstanding color.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||02-13-2000||10:34 AM||||Go on my web site and click on Fiero Photos and you will see a yellow GT just painted by my shop. <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net</A> ||||reg||7
Z||000004||bHooper||02-13-2000||12:03 PM||||Hey, Fieroshop, that yellow car looks beautifull!  Do you have any photos that I could use for my wallpaper?<P>BTW, my dreamcar is a yellow '88 GT with TTops! But a sunroof would be ok.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GREENDANO||02-13-2000||12:39 PM||||Here's my GT.  I just traded it a couple months ago.  The color is called Bright Yellow.  It's a PPG bright and bold color, I don't know the code.  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FinishedFiero.JPG"> <P>I miss that car.  Can't wait to drive the F40 though.  <BR>  Dan-O<p>[This message has been edited by GREENDANO (edited 02-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Robert||02-13-2000||02:22 PM||||I had my car painted 88 Fiero Yellow a few months ago.  The original color was silver.  I am very happy with the attention it gets, with my greatest achievement so far being parked in the front of a local yuppie restaurant by the valet parking guys.  It was ahead of a couple of Boxters and one BMW.  One thing to remember about a yellow car is that you have to wash it about every three days; this color really shows the dirt.<BR>Robert<BR>87 GT<P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mecar.jpg">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 02-13-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000007||Bens88GT||02-15-2000||01:31 AM||||I just picked up my first Fiero, a Yellow 88 GT w/sunroof, 3 days ago. So far it's attracted attention from passersby and everyone I know. Most people where I work didn't know what kind of car it was and were surprised that it was 12 years old. They thought it was brand new (it just got a brand new yellow paint job, it was originally black). Yellow looks great, though Robert is right, you must wash it often or it looks kinda dull.||||reg||14
Z||000008||88 Fiero||02-15-2000||02:08 PM||||The '88 Fiero Yellow is called 'Talbot Yellow"||||reg||1
Z||000009||SCCA FIERO||02-15-2000||06:42 PM||||Robert, that is a very sweet looking GT! ||||reg||14
